        "id": 1000024
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-16T16:47:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I just read your earlier comment. It looks like you tried this approach here: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/219334\n\nbut you said it still requires double-initialization. Sorry to be obtuse, but could you explain how it\u0027s different from ANGLETextureSharing?",
      "parentUuid": "7425d494_7bb6d865",
      "revId": "b3a98beb6a61c87bfa78e4ec69dc63ea4447d777",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "816d938b_0a7eb480",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/opengl/PhysicalDeviceGL.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000685
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-16T17:49:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we can pass some info here (like RequestAdapterOptions) indicating if we have that features required (or toggle enabled) then we can avoid double-initialization.\n\nDo we have access to what features is required at [`BackendGL::DiscoverPhysicalDevices`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/opengl/BackendGL.cpp;l\u003d56;drc\u003d04b384233ff1b695a826d1bc54b6ba4bec02aaca)\n\nIf so we can avoid the double-initialization using the feature approach.\n\nDifferent from ANGLETexgureSharing: I think it\u0027s that extensions availablity and toggles are cached at the the first `ContextEGL::Create`. They are inherited at the second `ContextEGL::Create` when actually creating the device. I don\u0027t really know details about ANGLETextureSharing, but I think that\u0027s the main issue",
      "parentUuid": "f4c7d63d_90ba36b7",
      "revId": "b3a98beb6a61c87bfa78e4ec69dc63ea4447d777",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9669f3c8_781450a3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/opengl/PhysicalDeviceGL.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 108,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000685
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-16T21:57:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For toggles, we can have Adapter stage toggle that naturally stays in RequestAdapterOptions and plumb that info through `dawn::native::Instance::EnumerateAdapters` -\u003e ... -\u003e `Backend::DiscoverPhysicalDevices` -\u003e `PhysicalDevice::Create` -\u003e `ContextEGL::Create`. (We already have the `DawnTogglesDescriptor` thing chained in RequestAdapterOptions)\n\nFor features, I\u0027m seeing `GetRequiredFeatures` is a device level call (inside `CreateDeviceImpl`) can we require features at adapter stage? (i.e. chain the required features info in `RequestAdapterOptions`)? If so we can do the same thing to avoid double-init (but we still need to pass that info through `ReqeustAdapterOptions`).\nTo me it seems we need to add a new `DawnFeaturesDescriptor` to `RequestAdapterOptions` to achieve the goal. Meanwhile we alrady have the whole `DawnTogglesDescriptor` setup.",
      "parentUuid": "816d938b_0a7eb480",
      "revId": "b3a98beb6a61c87bfa78e4ec69dc63ea4447d777",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
